    "type": "question",
    "label": "19",
    "prompt": "Out of eight competitors, five are chosen to compete in a final round. In the final round, three of the competitors are placed 1st, 2nd and 3rd. How many ways can this be done?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$3360$ ways.",
      "worked": "Choose the five finalists in $\\binom{8}{5}$ ways. From these five, assign 1st, 2nd and 3rd in $5\\times4\\times3$ ways.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=\\binom{8}{5}\\times5\\times4\\times3\\\\N&=56\\times60\\\\N&=3360.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
